{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"9b4a9e67a1a7458b6708587109219b88a754b8454b0f203a60e6e90298077eb3","slug":"publishing","location":"/guide/publishing.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Publishing a game (the player kit)","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Andrew Hutchings","given":"Andrew","family":"Hutchings"},"name":"Andrew Hutchings","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline","keywords":["amiga","emulator","ocs","ecs","rust"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/blob/main/docs/guide/publishing.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/CopperlineHQ/Copperline/edit/main/docs/guide/publishing.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"publishing.md","url":"/docs/build/publishing-9fe3249ca15a11579337cf78275d735e.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copperline can be built as a dedicated, launcher-free player for one game:\na small binary that boots straight into the title, with the machine model\nand RAM fixed at build time, no status bar, no debugger, and an in-game\nmenu carrying only what an end user of a shipped game changes -- CRT\nshader, bezel, fullscreen, controller setup, and (if the publisher opts\nin) save states. The distributable is a bundle: the player binary, the\ngame payload as a ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"W9No5jnqEk"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"sidecar file next to the binary","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"G7HPAEpdRf"}],"key":"qGbjz2HBEs"},{"type":"text","value":", the AROS boot ROM\npair, and the license documents.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"tQJbbMx7Dw"}],"key":"x4d4WWcf4P"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The payload is deliberately not embedded in the binary. The player stays\npure GPLv3 Copperline code and the game remains a separate work distributed\nalongside it (mere aggregation, the model commercial ScummVM releases use),\nso publishing a commercial title needs no license exception -- just passing\non the GPL text and a source link, which the kit generates.","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"dXP7cmfLjE"}],"key":"vSYTqMXadC"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The game manifest","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"nXMeYGBUPC"}],"identifier":"the-game-manifest","label":"The game manifest","html_id":"the-game-manifest","implicit":true,"key":"PyuDDzlEoq"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One TOML file describes the product; ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"JCqSfBxfjw"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crates/copperline-player/build.rs","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"pFbvxPtS6K"},{"type":"text","value":"\nbakes it into the binary as constants. The commented reference is\n","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"bK7qJ4cf84"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crates/copperline-player/game.example.toml","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"ROU8HbPyCw"},{"type":"text","value":":","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"ycDbbQOFjC"}],"key":"tW2HS2NanT"},{"type":"code","lang":"toml","value":"[game]\ntitle = \"Skyhawks\"           # window title\nid = \"skyhawks\"              # per-user save/settings directory name\nversion = \"1.2\"              # optional; names the bundle\n\n[payload]                    # exactly one payload kind\ncd = \"skyhawks.iso\"          # CD32/CDTV disc image (iso/cue/chd), or\n# adf = \"skyhawks.adf\"       # floppy in DF0, or\n# run = { files = \"amiga\", executable = \"Skyhawks\", args = \"\" }\n# sha256 = \"...\"             # optional integrity pin on the sidecar\n\n[machine]\nmodel = \"CD32\"               # any machine model: A500, A1200, CD32, ...\n# chip = \"2M\"                # optional RAM overrides on the profile\n# fast = \"8M\"\n\n[display]                    # defaults only; users change them in the menu\nshader = \"crt\"\nbezel = \"1084\"\nfullscreen = true\n\n[features]\nsave_states = false          # offer quick save/load slots in the menu\n\n[branding]\nicon = \"icon.png\"            # window/dock icon, replaces Copperline's","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"sK48m8q7pO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Payload kinds:","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"FUtNHckskV"}],"key":"eTAeltHqBO"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cd","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"dvt9YnBW3i"}],"key":"HOD3NS0ZuS"},{"type":"text","value":": the disc is in the machine’s CD drive at power-on and boots the\nway a real CD32/CDTV disc does. Saves persist through the console’s\nNVRAM, which lands in the per-game config directory.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"ms5vdwiZgj"}],"key":"Jki41bihLC"}],"key":"pckX2ubMkb"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"run","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"uIlavjHLGb"}],"key":"pbESqn1gMr"},{"type":"text","value":": an ordinary Amiga executable with its data files, booted the\nway ","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"xj1oZVCllc"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--run","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"V41j2P9QQs"},{"type":"text","value":" boots one (","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"RjfsTR1yKP"},{"type":"link","url":"/run","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Warp launch","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"NlCbWVrYvW"}],"urlSource":"run.md","dataUrl":"/run.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"BC9bF1JMGT"},{"type":"text","value":"), warp-booting to the program’s load.\nOn first launch the files tree is copied into the per-game config\ndirectory; guest writes land in the copy, so saves persist and survive\nupdates: an updated payload removes members it no longer carries,\nre-copies its own, and leaves everything else alone. Updates are\ndetected by each member’s size and timestamp plus the manifest’s\nversion and pin -- so bump ","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"eEJryo35vu"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[game] version","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"LJloRTekzf"},{"type":"text","value":" (or pin the payload) when\nshipping an update, and the staged copy refreshes even if the archive\npreserved every timestamp.","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"jVDjsCuEST"}],"key":"ndUi9Oe97W"}],"key":"yO2pD31Xsf"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"adf","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"k47Nheaipe"}],"key":"oGOSRXHHB3"},{"type":"text","value":": the image is in DF0 at power-on, also from a per-user copy so\nthe guest can write to it.","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"S7nXMWOLfW"}],"key":"v4rwqwizHH"}],"key":"DXyfgB59zF"}],"key":"HiAdXn8xPS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional ","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"PBDHESyzjJ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sha256","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"aVPHHEL3Qd"},{"type":"text","value":" pins the payload: the player refuses to start when\nthe sidecar does not match, so a bundle cannot be quietly retargeted at a\ndifferent disc. Leave it out to let the payload be patched without\nrebuilding the player. It applies to file payloads only.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"puBpM5rote"}],"key":"Pak4DFNU1B"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Building and bundling","position":{"start":{"line":76,